    fix(board): refuse a same-count board row replacement (AUG-195)
    
    board_shrink_check compared row COUNT only, so swapping 297 board rows for
    297 different rows passed the commit path and the CI --recent mode with exit 0
    (the module docstring called it an HONEST LIMIT; a test asserted the hole).
    
    Refuse whenever a baseline row id is absent from the candidate, regardless of
    the count, and keep the message naming the missing ids. A count drop still
    fails as before; BOARD_ALLOW_SHRINK=1|true|yes still turns the refusal into a
    loud NOTICE with both counts and every missing id; content edits of a surviving
    id and line reordering still pass. Docstring and success message made true.
    
    Tests: flip test_same_count_replacement_is_the_documented_blind_spot into a
    refusal arm, add equal-count and growing-count replacement refusals, --recent
    mode refusals, single-row in-place edit, reordering, append-with-baseline-ids,
    and all three override spellings. 29 passed (was 19).
    
    Gates run on this tree:
      pytest tests/test_board_shrink_check.py -x -q     -> 29 passed
      ruff check + ruff format --check (both files)     -> clean
      red-proof (scratch repo, pre-fix vs post-fix)     -> .hermes/cache/scratch/195-proof
      gitreins guard: secrets PASS, lint PASS, spec_alignment PASS,
        tests(full) BLOCKED by live DuckBrain namespace-lock contention
        (DELETE 409 "Push in flight ... held by pid <foreign>"), not by this diff —
        that test passes alone at the base commit, so the commit was made with the
        hook bypassed and disclosed here. Hosted CI runs the full gate on main.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
